{"schema_version":"1.8.0","id":"OESA-2026-3283","published":"2026-08-07T02:43:33Z","modified":"2026-08-07T03:00:57.032765217Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-22185"],"summary":"lmdb security update","details":"Symas LMDB is an extraordinarily fast, memory-efficient database we developed for the OpenLDAP Project. With memory-mapped files, it has the read performance of a pure in-memory database while retaining the persistence of standard disk-based databases.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nOpenLDAP Lightning Memory-Mapped Database (LMDB) versions up to and including 0.9.14, prior to commit 8e1fda8, contain a heap buffer underflow in the readline() function of mdb_load. When processing malformed input containing an embedded NUL byte, an unsigned offset calculation can underflow and cause an out-of-bounds read of one byte before the allocated heap buffer. This can cause mdb_load to crash, leading to a limited denial-of-service condition.(CVE-2026-22185)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"lmdb","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/lmdb&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["lmdb-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","lmdb-debuginfo-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","lmdb-debugsource-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","lmdb-devel-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["lmdb-help-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["lmdb-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["lmdb-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","lmdb-debuginfo-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","lmdb-debugsource-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","lmdb-devel-0.9.31-3.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3283.json"}},{"package":{"name":"lmdb","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/lmdb&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.9.31-3.oe2403sp3"}